  "source_findings": [
    {
      "area": "Private ABI/ownership",
      "finding": "Private header and 12 useful register/calculation leaves; no new owner, dispatcher, service state, allocation or ordinary polling-object fields. Public SPI header and private provider.h retain baseline bytes. spi.c directly uses the leaves and retains wait/drain/quiet/retained-fault policy and transfer byte loop."
    },
    {
      "area": "Boundedness",
      "finding": "Every leaf finishes after a fixed number of CPU operations/MMIO accesses. cs_driven scans at most 16 pins; divider selects 2..256 in at most 7 steps. No leaf polls to eventual completion, waits, drains RX, invokes fault ownership or adds fallback async polling. W1 adds no async or DMA path."
    },
    {
      "area": "CSUSP register semantics",
      "finding": "suspend_once retains CR1 RMW semantics, explicitly excludes CSTART when setting CSUSP and issues DSB, so it cannot retrigger transfer. CSUSP is a read-as-zero command; the corrected new test uses model suspend_request rather than readable CSUSP=1."
    },
    {
      "area": "Stop proof",
      "finding": "stopped is a non-clearing snapshot: CSTART clear and either SUSP, or finite TSIZE>0 with EOT+TXC. TSIZE=0 is not completion. It does not claim quiet. Existing polling wrappers still enforce stop -> quiet -> RX drain -> disable."
    },
    {
      "area": "Disable/final access",
      "finding": "disable acknowledges SUSP before SPE=0, issues DSB, then proves CR1 and FIFO state. Its private contract retains caller-owned stopped/quiet/drained preconditions. Existing synchronous owner retains waits and faults; extraction promises no stronger timeout/completion contract."
    },
    {
      "area": "CS and SCK park order",
      "finding": "release_cs proves GPIO output/high ODR before clearing held-CS ownership; failure retains the pointer. Wrapper keeps CS high before SCK idle-latch/GPIO-output parking and checked reset. sck_idle writes the output latch before mode change. AF/pin checks and ordering remain unchanged."
    },
    {
      "area": "Clock/calculations",
      "finding": "clock_ready retains gate/mux/profile checks, revision-V guard before HSICFGR, default HSI trim64 and bounded high-profile checks. Divider retains 65/32.5/99.45MHz envelopes and output-on-success semantics. quiet_us retains ceil(divisor*1000000/nominal_clock)+2; calculated budget is not a measured SCK qualification."
    },
    {
      "area": "Mechanical equivalence",
      "finding": "Independently removed comments/whitespace and normalized extracted names: pins_ready, cs_driven, sck_alternate, sck_idle, clock_ready, reset and release_cs match old bodies exactly. Inspected the remaining five leaves and driver callers for equivalent expressions/preconditions. Driver wait and byte-transfer loop remain byte-identical."
    },
    {
      "area": "Link/SDK closure",
      "finding": "SoC CMake selects helper TU with SPI modes. All maintained direct spi.c test consumers receive it, including flash/RAM closure and I2C long-factory, without weakening assertions. Descriptor adds only private helper source/header payload. Empty selects neither SPI TU. No clean installed-SDK run is claimed."
    },
    {
      "area": "Scope",
      "finding": "No DMA stream/request/IRQ implementation, public ABI expansion, additional ordinary owner state, hardware qualification or IO27 status change. This polling-helper extraction only prepares for separately reviewed finite DMA work."
    }
  ],
